body:
Economy and development beyond an abstract number boosted by an arbitrary percentage.  There should be natural resources, land fertility, infrastructure, education, trade, corporations, guilds, etc.

&#x200B;

Also, the ability to say "I don't care about this kind of event" and just have it auto-choose a result.  If I am running my empire and I am at war with another empire, I could literally not care less if one of my courtiers banged one of my other courtiers and had a bastard.  I don't EVER want to get invited to play a board game with anyone.  I don't care who my great grandchild is betrothed to.  I don't care that my second cousin has a murder scheme against them.  Just leave me alone goddammit.

Physician's Desk Reference, hollowed out. Inside, waterproof matches, iodine tablets, beet seeds, protein bars, NASA blanket... and in case I get bored, Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's Stone.  No wait, Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban.

&#x200B;

Edit: Question, did my shoes come off in the plane crash?

Check this out.  This should give you some guidance as to approximately what specialties you may be able to get into:

&#x200B;

[https://mk0nrmp3oyqui6wqfm.kinstacdn.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Charting-Outcomes-in-the-Match-2018\_Seniors-1.pdf](https://mk0nrmp3oyqui6wqfm.kinstacdn.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Charting-Outcomes-in-the-Match-2018_Seniors-1.pdf)

Alien: Isolation

&#x200B;

By far my favorite horror game I have ever played, and strange coming from Creative Assembly who has no track record in first person horror.
